			"date": "2025-07-21T22:30:00.083Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>cbirdsong</span></a></span> Temporal seems to use RFC 9557 which is a much stricter date format <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Temporal/Instant#rfc_9557_format\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">developer.mozilla.org/en-US/do</span><span class=\"invisible\">cs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Temporal/Instant#rfc_9557_format</span></a></p><p>so, we could absolutely support that one too but it doesn’t really solve a problem 😓</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
